diff --git a/docs/PRIVACY-AND-AUDITS.md b/docs/PRIVACY-AND-AUDITS.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f948694
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/PRIVACY-AND-AUDITS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,82 @@
+# Privacy and service review
+
+## Data inventory
+
+| Data | Purpose | Location | Retention/deletion |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Random session ID | Find requested bookmarks | HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Strict cookie scoped to `/devtools-times/` | 24-hour cookie; deleted when clearing the list |
+| Up to 100 published article IDs | Reading list requested by visitor | Server session storage | Inaccessible after 24 hours from last change; deletion endpoint removes storage |
+| Username/password | None | Not collected; demo provider removed | None |
+| Analytics, search terms, advertising profiles | None | Not collected | None |
+| Connection and infrastructure logs | Deliver and operate the application | Hosting infrastructure, outside application control | Operator must configure minimization and deletion |
+
+The session contains no account profile, credential, IP address, or browsing history.
+Opening a page or an empty reading list does not create a session. Responses are
+private and not cacheable. JSON writes require a same-origin Origin header,
+validated article ID, and a bounded body. Deleting the final bookmark destroys
+the session. HTTPS is mandatory for production; Secure cookies intentionally do
+not support plain HTTP production browsing.
+
+## Production storage and retention
+
+The configured Node filesystem driver stores sessions under `.astro/sessions`
+relative to the working directory. Framework TTL prevents reads after expiry.
+The application physically purges expired files on startup and hourly, so files
+can remain for up to one additional hour. The session directory is restricted to
+the process owner (0700). A stopped application cannot perform cleanup; run
+`node scripts/purge-sessions.mjs` during shutdown/decommissioning if needed. Use
+the same working directory for the server and cleanup command. Storage must be
+encrypted and excluded from source control and backups. If a shared
+store is used, require encryption in transit and at rest, least-privilege service
+credentials, native TTL, and verified deletion. Do not log request bodies, cookies,
+credentials, or full request URLs containing personal information. Limit hosting
+access logs to operational need and set an explicit short retention period.
+
+The application cannot configure hosting encryption, logs, TLS termination, or
+backups. Deployment owners must verify these before exposing production traffic.
+Reverse proxies must preserve security headers and disable shared caching for HTML
+and API responses. Static files bypass application middleware; set equivalent
+nosniff and resource policy headers at the hosting layer.
+
+## Third-party register
+
+| Integration | Status | Review evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Demo credential service | Removed; accounts unavailable | No independent evidence supplied |
+| Remote analytics and advertising scripts | Disabled, blocked by CSP | No independent evidence supplied |
+| Google Fonts | Removed; system fonts used | No visitor disclosure |
+| Remote image hosts | Replaced with bundled images | No visitor disclosure |
+| Hosting provider | Operator controlled; review required | Must be supplied by deployment owner |
+
+There is no completed independent third-party audit or certification. Automated
+dependency scans are useful checks and are not independent audits.
+
+## Required review before any service activation
+
+The service owner must create a dated review record including:
+
+- Service, owner, purpose, exact fields transferred, and why each field is necessary.
+- Processing locations, subprocessors, transfer terms, and applicable agreements.
+- Retention, deletion API/procedure, backup deletion, and evidence deletion was tested.
+- Encryption, access controls, breach notification, and incident response contact.
+- Independent audit report or assessment (scope, date, auditor, findings, remediation).
+- Approval owner/date, expiration within 12 months, and evidence references.
+
+Keep vendor reports and secrets out of this public repository. Record only a safe
+reference to restricted evidence. Re-review annually, on material integration or
+subprocessor changes, and after incidents. Block activation on missing evidence
+or unresolved critical/high findings. Re-enabling an integration requires a code
+review of its data flow, policy text, and the exact CSP allowlist change; there
+is deliberately no runtime switch that loads the former demo services.
+
+Commission an independent application review before production launch and at least
+annually thereafter. Scope must include credential lifecycle if accounts return,
+CSRF, XSS and CSP, session isolation/expiry/deletion, dependency findings, logging,
+storage, and vendor disclosures. Assign findings, remediate, and obtain retest
+evidence. Do not present this checklist as proof an audit happened.
+
+## Checks
+
+`pnpm build && pnpm test:security` checks production HTTP responses without a browser.
+`pnpm audit --audit-level=high` scans the locked dependency tree. CI runs both on
+changes and weekly. Triage findings and review fixes before merging.
